body:
Oh, i managed to fix it for myself now, without disabling optimization!

Firstly, i have added...
```
#pragma optimize("", off)
bool TriangleMesh::intersect_ray(const Vector3 &p_begin, const Vector3 &p_dir, Vector3 &r_point, Vector3 &r_normal) const {
// ...
}
#pragma optimize("", on)
```
... these pragmas around intersect_ray method to disable any kind of compiler optimization for it.

Secondly, i have changed one thing in `spatial_editor_gizmos.cpp`.

Earlier it was:
```
		if (collision_mesh->intersect_ray(ray_from, ray_dir, rpos, rnorm)) {
			r_pos = gt.xform(rpos);
			r_normal = gt.basis.xform(rnorm).normalized();
			return true;
		}
```

I changed it over:
```
		volatile auto ray = collision_mesh->intersect_ray(ray_from, ray_dir, rpos, rnorm);
		if (ray) {
			r_pos = gt.xform(rpos);
			r_normal = gt.basis.xform(rnorm).normalized();
			return true;
		}
```

Dirty changes, but writing it for anybody else who could have it too.
